# Not an expression-mode bug -- reproduces identically in plain command-mode calls
# (`$f 5 2`) -- but found while testing expression-mode closure signatures, so
# recorded here rather than lost. A closure parameter with a default value can be
# omitted, and can be overridden by name, but overriding it positionally (supplying
# every parameter, including the defaulted one, as a plain unnamed argument) fails
# with "Stray unnamed argument" instead of binding normally.

$add := {|$x $y = 10| ($x + $y)}
$result := $($add 5 2)
assert ($result == 7) "a positional argument should be able to override a parameter's default value"
